+---
+id: dl-002-applypatch-semantics-clone-input-atomic-strict-validation
+type: decision-log
+title: "applyPatch semantics: clone input, atomic, strict validation"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+## Context
+
+RFC 6902 leaves some behaviours open: failure handling, removing the root, and aliasing of values.
+
+## Decision
+
+- The input document is deep-cloned first and patch values are cloned on insertion, so neither the
+  document nor the patch is mutated or aliased; a failing patch throws and returns nothing (atomic).
+- Invalid patches (not an array, unknown `op`, missing/non-string `path` or `from`, missing `value`)
+  throw before any operation is applied.
+- `remove` of the root throws; `move` into its own child throws; `-` works only for `add`.
+- `test` uses JSON equality: object key order is ignored, array order matters, types are strict.
+- Members are set with `defineProperty`, so `__proto__` is an ordinary key; lookups reuse the
+  own-members-only rules of `resolvePointer`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Callers get a safe, all-or-nothing update at the cost of one deep clone per call.
